      "text": "taught them as one having authority, Matt. 7:29. he said unto them, Have ye not read what David did, Matt. 12:3. Why speakest thou unto them in parables, Matt. 13:10. Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, Matt. 22:29. preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God, Mark 1:14. entered into the synagogue, and taught, Mark 1:21. preached the word unto them, Mark 2:2. all these things are done in parables, Mark 4:11. he began to teach them, that the Son of man, Mark 8:31. they were astonished … for his word was with power, Luke 4:32. when Jesus perceived their thoughts, he answering said, Luke 5:22. Tell me therefore, which of them will love him most, Luke 7:42. our heart burn within us, while he talked with us, Luke 24:32. he whom God hath sent speaketh the words of God, John 3:34. My doctrine is not mine, but his that sent me, John 7:16. wrote on the ground, as though he heard them not, John 8:6. even as the Father said unto me, so I speak, John 12:50. He saith unto him the third time, John 21:17.",
